      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what you mean about the weight, but it doesn't feel like something someone can just help me carry. it feels more fundamental than that. like, if you look at the math of it, if everything is eventually going to end and nothing we do actually leaves a permanent mark, then the difference between existing and not existing is basically zero. it's just a neutral equation. why is it considered \"brave\" to struggle against a math problem that's already been solved?",
